// GROUP "new" — the frozen tool block on a forced turn (orchestration.stableToolBlock "freeze",
// commit 1d3209a).
//
// Frozen, the forced orchestration calls send the warmed full tool block instead of switching to a
// tool subset (live probe E7: 8.3 s per switch, two switches per forced turn); the subset is enforced
// where the call is dispatched instead. A call outside it is refused and logged as
// tool_restriction_refused, and each refusal costs one warm iteration — the config comment says to
// watch it, and to turn freeze off if refusals are frequent. This scenario keeps them few on a turn
// that is both forced and planned, and checks the turn still delivers the documented fact.
//
// The turn is FORCED when the up-front source judge flags the question (requiresDelegatedResearch,
// agent/turn-setup.ts:193) — that verdict is asserted, so a run where the turn was not forced fails
// on its premise instead of passing vacuously. While no plan exists the forced allowlist offers
// record_plan once (agent/forced-orchestration-tools.ts), so the turn is planned as well.
//
// Events asserted, emitters verified in packages/core/src:
//   guardrail_flagged {type: "upfront_source_sensitive_detected", answered, decidedBy?}
//                                                    agent/runtime.ts:1901-1903
//   tool_restriction_refused {tool, reason ("must_orchestrate" | "discovery_withheld"), iteration,
//                             allowedCount}          agent/runtime.ts:4198
// Ground truth (eval/e2e/ENVIRONMENT.md, /dokumentation.html): NW-3104 on the NW-LG 18 charges from
// 0 to 80 % in 38 minutes (full in 61).
{
  id: "new-frozen-tool-block-forced-turn",
  title: "On a forced, planned turn the frozen tool block refuses few calls and the turn delivers the documented fact",
  group: "new",
  tags: ["tool-block", "forced", "site", "slow"],
  description: "Guards stableToolBlock \"freeze\" (1d3209a): on a turn the source judge forces to orchestrate, calls outside the forced subset are refused at the call site (tool_restriction_refused) instead of the tool array switching. Refusals must stay at 2 or fewer — more means the trade costs warm iterations — and the turn must still complete with the page's answer (38 minutes) from a research specialist.",
  requires: ["model", "e2e-site"],
  identity: "eval",
  timeoutMs: 900000,
  steps: [
    {
      kind: "turn",
      id: "forced-doc-fact",
      message: "Wie lange braucht der Akku-Pack NW-3104 am Schnellladegerät NW-LG 18, um von 0 auf 80 % zu laden? Maßgeblich ist die Dokumentation unter http://www.nordlicht-werkzeuge.test/dokumentation.html --auto",
      effort: "medium",
      timeoutMs: 600000,
      expect: {
        status: "ok",
        reply: {
          // "38 Minuten", "38 min", "38 Min.", "38 minutes".
          matches: ["\\b38\\s*min"],
          minChars: 15,
        },
        events: {
          must: [
            // The premise: the turn was forced to orchestrate.
            { type: "guardrail_flagged", where: { "data.type": "upfront_source_sensitive_detected" }, min: 1 },
            // The frozen block's cost stays small.
            { type: "tool_restriction_refused", min: 0, max: 2 },
          ],
        },
        agents: { mustRunAny: ["researcher", "browser_agent", "source_verifier", "summarizer"] },
      },
    },
  ],
}
